              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "categoryId": "silhouette",
            "strongestReasonBelowThree": "The boss/cheek kink in plan is only softened, not removed, and the boss outline is faceted.",
            "resolved": true,
            "resolutionEvidence": [
              {
                "kind": "technical-record",
                "recordId": "polish-r24/independent-review.json",
                "observation": "George explicitly accepted the softened kink. r24 has zero alpha changes against r23 in all 13 views, and the major contours are unchanged at gameplay scale. The facets show only at close range.",
                "evidenceSha256": "755ed8ad86c740b0e43edc40fa3e63f83853f181f002d6130113820d19ea8e30"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "categoryId": "mechanical-coherence",
            "strongestReasonBelowThree": "Carried from r22: the fixed flange was parented to the articulated ball, and there is no posed evidence. New for r24: the bolts could be floating, buried or clipped by the floor boolean, as happened in r23. Also carried: the inboard wedge shard at the spot-face.",
            "resolved": true,
            "resolutionEvidence": [
              {
                "kind": "technical-record",
                "recordId": "polish-r24/independent-review.json",
                "observation": "From r23 onward, P06 (ring, bolts, collar) is parented to M.turret and P09 moves alone, which resolves the parenting. Bolts are created after the floor clip, with their rear faces exactly on the ring face (x 1.116), radially inside the ring annulus and above the clip plane (min z 0.1405 against 0.045). The close-ups show them seated with no gap. The wedge shard is unchanged and was deliberately not selected by George; it is a known residual, not a regression. Posed ball evidence is still absent, but no articulation limits are declared, so it is a coverage gap for a later animation gate, not a static-structure defect.",
                "evidenceSha256": "755ed8ad86c740b0e43edc40fa3e63f83853f181f002d6130113820d19ea8e30"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "categoryId": "production-integrity",
            "strongestReasonBelowThree": "Carried from r22: there is no hash-bound deterministic evaluator result, so the rubric gate fails closed. The triangle budget is nearly exhausted (49,982 of 50,000). One bolt probe view (profile) is uninformative.",
            "resolved": true,
            "resolutionEvidence": [
              {
                "kind": "technical-record",
                "recordId": "polish-r24/independent-review.json",
                "observation": "I judged this from technical evidence, as instructed. Validation passed and is deterministic, renders are identical to the baseline, dimensions pass 37/37, native isolation is complete, and the budget is within limit. All of it is bound to checkpoint 53ea7c63...74fa. The thin headroom is a constraint, not a violation. Caveat: under AGENTS.md, a visual go still requires the deterministic evaluator's exact 'go' on the complete r24 assessment, which the producer is running in parallel. Until that result exists, the gate stays fail-closed regardless of this review.",
                "evidenceSha256": "755ed8ad86c740b0e43edc40fa3e63f83853f181f002d6130113820d19ea8e30"
